      "writtenOn": "2023-05-29T10:05:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the default proxy?\nDoes it means the global proxy or the proxy of default network?\nFrom the (very confusing) documentation,\n\"Retrieve the global HTTP proxy, or if no global HTTP proxy is set, a\n network-specific HTTP proxy.  If {@code network} is null, the\n network-specific proxy returned is the proxy of the default active\n network.\"\nIt seems to me this will return the proxy info of default network since the global proxy is not set. If so, is it better to:\n  1. name it unstartedDefaultNetworkProxyInfo to be more clear?\n  2. avoid using the term \"default proxy\"?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11303,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 11303,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "e34c78f4a2a28c69059860a6e36827edab6ab14c",
